1. DEFINITIONS

"Platform" means the Kryptos Tēs Moiras software, services, server
infrastructure, repositories, storage systems, Copilot systems,
artificial intelligence components, documentation, binaries, and
associated materials, to the extent owned or controlled by the
respective rights holders.

"Licensor" means the person or legal entity holding the applicable
rights to the relevant component of the Platform.

"User" means any individual or entity accessing, downloading,
installing, executing, or using the Platform.

"Private Repository" means a repository designated as private and
accessible only to its owner and explicitly authorized collaborators.

"Confidential Information" means non-public source code, cryptographic
keys, authentication credentials, recovery tokens, internal
architectural details, security mechanisms, vulnerability information,
private repository contents, and other information designated as
confidential or reasonably understood to be confidential.

"Copilot" means the account-specific code analysis and assistance
system associated with a User.

"Central AI" means the artificial intelligence system responsible for
assisting with internal Platform processes, analyzing technical
artifacts, assessing reported problems, and proposing solutions.

"Published Component" means a component whose source code or binary
has been explicitly made publicly available by its rights holder.

"Authorized Action" means an operation expressly permitted by the
applicable service rules, the User's permissions, and applicable law.


